<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle market quiet, no trade - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle market quiet, no trade - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading on slaughter steers and heifers was at a standstill, USDA said. Large weekly movement of 99,800 cleaned up showlists and put packer live inventories in good shape.</p>
<p>Live basis sales - Equivalent 3 percent shrink delivered and FOB, some FOB 4% shrink. Dressed basis delivered ( paid on hot carcass weights)</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers -  No reported sales.</p>
<p>Slaughter heifers - No reported sales.</p>
<p>Confirmed - None  Last Week - 400  Last Year - 400</p>
<p>For week -  None. Sm Pd Lst Wk - None.  Sm Pd Lst Yr - None.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
